# Keep Project Context Current

The file `.cursor/plans/project-context.md` is the **single source of truth** for this
project. It must be comprehensive enough that if all chat history were lost, an AI could
fully understand what this project is, how it works, and what state it is in — solely
from this file.

## Read It First

At the start of every session, read `.cursor/plans/project-context.md` before doing any work.

## When to Update

After ANY of these changes, update the relevant section of `project-context.md` before
ending your turn:

- New files or scripts added, renamed, or removed
- New external system integrations (APIs, databases, services)
- New database tables, schemas, or stored procedures
- Changes to orchestration flows (Prefect deployments, schedules)
- New automation schedules or cron jobs
- Architectural shifts or design decisions
- Directory structure changes
- Credential or secret management changes
- Files moved to `_archive/`

## What Does NOT Require an Update

- Bug fixes that don't change project scope
- Comment edits or formatting changes
- Minor refactors that don't alter architecture or file layout

## How to Update

- Keep the existing section structure — don't reorganize unless asked
- Be factual and terse — this is a reference doc, not a narrative
- Update the "Last updated" date when making changes
- Never delete content without replacing it with the corrected/updated version
- The file must always be a complete and accurate snapshot of the project

## The Standard

Ask yourself: *"If someone wiped the chat history and opened this project cold, would
`project-context.md` tell them everything they need to know?"* If not, update it.
